  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 215 PM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nCool and dry days are in store for Tuesday and Wednesday while\nshortwave upper ridging passes west to east across TX. The stable\nperiod will be short-lived and broader the zonal flow pattern over\nthe southern CONUS only allows for the sun to visit for about a\nday or so before low level moisture thickens back over the region.\nBy Wednesday evening, deepening moisture brings a few streamer\nshowers back with the upper pattern turning more southwesterly in\nadvance of the next southern US upper trough. Surface ridging\nremain entrenched over the Deep South and some coastal troughing\ncould also combine with this pattern to bring enough lift for\noverrunning light showers. Temperatures will gradually migrate \nback to more seasonable values late in the week while the skies \nremain mostly cloudy to cloudy. Over the weekend another backdoor \nstyle cold front is expected to arrive and have another shortwave \nbring more overrunning rains.",
